   "tip": {
    "title": "No 'is' needed",
    "text": "Odia often leaves out 'is' in simple statements: ମୋ ନାଁ ରିନା (my name Rina), ମୁଁ ସୀତା (I Sita). Notice also the two 'your's: ଆପଣଙ୍କ ନାଁ for an adult stranger, ତୁମ ନାଁ for a child — Rina switches when she talks to Prakash's son."
